  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 106 AM CDT Fri Jul 17 2026\n\nAs of 1 AM CDT, temperatures around the area are in the mid to\nupper 70s with winds out of the southeast around 10 mph. \nTemperatures today are expected to rise once again into the 90s \nwith heat index values in the upper 90s to around 100 degrees. \nThe NBM has been a little overdone the last few days so dropped \nhighs just a little over northern SD and east of the James \nValley. A Heat Advisory has been issued for portions of central \nand northeast SD from 1 to 9 PM CDT.\n\nA low and corresponding cold front will make its way across the area \nthis afternoon bringing northerly winds to the area a slight cool \ndown Saturday. Heat is expected to return Sunday and Monday. \nFollowing this, temperatures should moderate for the rest of the \nwork week. A warm front will move across the area Sunday bringing a \nchance showers and thunderstorms. There is a 20-30% chance across \nnorth central SD during the morning hours and then across central \nand northeast SD during the evening to early overnight hours. No \nsevere weather is expected at this time. The HRRR Smoke model is \nshowing a plume of elevated smoke heading south out of Canada and \ninto our area by mid afternoon. No surface smoke is expected at this \ntime. The only impact looks to be a slight milky look to the sky. \nWith this prolonged period of dry and warm weather, fuels have been \ndrying out. Winds for the next few days don't look to be overly \nstrong, gusts up to 25 mph, so fire concerns are low. However, \nMonday, with the Sunday low still over some of our east central \ncounties, we are expecting some higher wind gusts which will \nelevated fire concerns, depending on how much precipitation, if any, \nwe get with the possible storms Sunday.",
